<title>USA: Mobil sees U.S. Gulf oilfields up by weekend.</title>
<headline>Mobil sees U.S. Gulf oilfields up by weekend.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mobil Corp said Friday it expects production back up by the weekend at six oilfields it shut-in Thursday because of Hurricane Danny.</p>
<p>Workers are returning to Eugene Island 240, Green Canyon 18/60, Ship Shoal 72 and Ship Shoal 182 on Friday, the Mobil spokesman said.</p>
<p>Workers at Main Pass fields 6/103 and 73 will return on Saturday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are anticipating that over the weekend all of these operations will be back into production,&quot; the spokesman said.</p>
<p>The six fields concerned are among the smaller ones in the various systems they feed into. Most big producers in the Gulf did not shut in production as the Hurricane passed through.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
